# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere, on every OS.
#
# Why: without this, Windows checkouts materialize CRLF
# (`core.autocrlf=true`) while oxfmt writes LF, so every `pnpm format`
# rewrote every file's line endings ("no changes" that still dirtied the
# tree) until the next checkout flipped them back. Pinning `eol=lf` makes
# the checkout, the formatter, and the repo blobs agree, so format is a
# true no-op on clean files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only launchers must stay CRLF to execute.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never convert, never diff.
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
